You are working in a Python FastAPI marketplace project.

Global rules:
- Do not generate production code without explicit interfaces or repository/service boundaries.
- Prefer test-first or test-alongside-development workflow for any non-trivial change.
- Every business rule change must include unit or integration tests.
- Keep controllers thin and move business logic into services.
- Do not couple services directly to raw database driver calls when a repository abstraction exists.
- Preserve API contracts unless a task explicitly requests a breaking change.
- Prefer deterministic tests with mocks or mongomock over external dependencies.
- Generate coverage-friendly tests and keep CI artifacts up to date.
- Do not delete or rewrite demo data unless the user explicitly asks for it.
